use std
into drum3d.amni
lang amni
Amni-Drive's 3D Cylindrical Rolling Dash Dial physics and perspective projection engine. Primary apps sit on a massive horizontal-axis cylindrical drum recessed into the dashboard; swiping vertically (or horizontally) spins the drum with spring-damped inertia so the active app rolls into the dash slot while the next app rolls smoothly into primary view. All float math uses 32-bit floats.
Constants: `SLOT_STEP_DEG` is 46.0 (angular spacing between adjacent app faces on the drum), `NUM_APPS` is 4 (0 Amni-Map 3D, 1 Spotify Media, 2 Voice & Apps, 3 Vehicle Telemetry).
Struct `DrumState` holds `angle_deg` and `vel_deg` as 32-bit floats, `active_idx` as a 32-bit integer, and `dragging` as a boolean.
Struct `DrumFace` holds `app_idx` as a 32-bit integer, `rel_deg` as a 32-bit float, `y_center` as a 32-bit float, `vis_h` as a 32-bit float, `vis_w` as a 32-bit float, `shade` as a 32-bit float (0.0 recessed dark to 1.0 full front illumination), `z_depth` as a 32-bit float, and `visible` as a boolean.
Function `wrap_rel_deg` takes `deg` as a 32-bit float and wraps it into the symmetric range `[-total/2, total/2)` where `total = f32(NUM_APPS) * SLOT_STEP_DEG` (184.0 degrees).
Function `drum_swipe` takes a mutable `DrumState` `st`, `delta_px` and `viewport_h` as 32-bit floats; marks `st.dragging = true`, converts `delta_px` to angular rotation `d_deg = (delta_px / max(viewport_h, 200.0)) * 95.0`, adds `d_deg` to `st.angle_deg`, and sets `st.vel_deg = d_deg * 24.0`.
Function `drum_release` takes a mutable `DrumState` `st`; sets `st.dragging = false`, projects stopping angle `proj = st.angle_deg + st.vel_deg * 0.14`, rounds `proj / SLOT_STEP_DEG` to the nearest integer `slot`, and sets `st.active_idx` to `((slot % NUM_APPS) + NUM_APPS) % NUM_APPS`.
Function `drum_step` takes a mutable `DrumState` `st` and `dt` as 32-bit floats (clamped to `[0.001, 0.05]`). When `st.dragging` is false, compute the nearest detent target angle `target = round(st.angle_deg / SLOT_STEP_DEG) * SLOT_STEP_DEG`, apply critically damped spring acceleration `acc = (target - st.angle_deg) * 140.0 - st.vel_deg * 21.0`, add `acc * dt` to `st.vel_deg` and `st.vel_deg * dt` to `st.angle_deg`, snap directly to `target` with zero velocity when `abs(target - st.angle_deg) < 0.08` and `abs(st.vel_deg) < 0.4`, and update `st.active_idx` to `((int(round(st.angle_deg / SLOT_STEP_DEG)) % NUM_APPS) + NUM_APPS) % NUM_APPS`.
Function `drum_project_face` takes `app_idx` as a 32-bit integer, `roll_deg` as a 32-bit float, `stage_x`, `stage_y`, `stage_w`, and `stage_h` as 32-bit floats, returning a `DrumFace`.
Compute `rel = wrap_rel_deg(f32(app_idx) * SLOT_STEP_DEG - roll_deg)`. If `abs(rel)` is at least 78.0 degrees, return a `DrumFace` with `visible = false`.
Convert `rad = rel * 0.0174532925`. Let `drum_r = stage_h * 0.62`, `focal = stage_h * 1.45`.
Compute 3D cylindrical point on the barrel: `y3 = drum_r * sin(rad)` and recess depth `z3 = drum_r * (1.0 - cos(rad))` (0 at dead-center front, increasing as the dial rolls back into the dash!).
Perspective projection scale: `persp = focal / (focal + z3)`.
Compute projected screen center `y_center = stage_y + stage_h * 0.5 + y3 * persp`, projected face height `vis_h = (stage_h * 0.58) * max(0.08, cos(rad)) * persp`, projected face width `vis_w = (stage_w * 0.86) * (0.86 + 0.14 * persp)` (edges curve inward slightly as the drum rolls away into the dash!), and cylindrical shading `shade = clamp(pow(max(0.0, cos(rad)), 1.35) * 0.88 + 0.12, 0.10, 1.0)`. Return `DrumFace` with `visible = true` and `z_depth = z3`.
